## Test Naming Conventions

### Pattern
```
should [expected behavior] when [condition]
```

### Examples
```typescript
// Good
it('should return 404 when ticket does not exist')
it('should create ticket with status backlog by default')
it('should throw ForbiddenException when user lacks permission')
it('should display loading spinner while fetching')

// Bad
it('test ticket creation')
it('works correctly')
it('handles error')
```

## Coverage Guidelines

### Targets (MVP)
- Services: 80%+
- Controllers: 60%+ (mostly covered by integration tests)
- Components: 60%+ (behavior, not template details)
- Utilities: 90%+
- Repositories: Covered by integration tests

### Running Coverage
```bash
# Backend
pnpm --filter server test:cov

# Frontend
pnpm --filter client test:cov
```

### What to Ignore
```typescript
// Add to jest config
coveragePathIgnorePatterns: [
  '/node_modules/',
  '.module.ts',      // NestJS modules are just wiring
  '.dto.ts',         // DTOs are just types
  'main.ts',         // Bootstrap file
  '/test/',          // Test utilities
]
```

## Mocking Best Practices

### DO Mock
- External services (HTTP, database)
- Time (`jest.useFakeTimers()`)
- Random values when testing specific outputs
- Side effects (logging, analytics)

### DON'T Mock
- Pure functions
- The system under test
- Simple data transformations

### Partial Mocks
```typescript
// When you only need to mock some methods
const partialMock = {
  ...actualService,
  specificMethod: jest.fn(),
};
```

## Async Testing

```typescript
// Prefer async/await over done callback
it('should fetch data', async () => {
  const result = await service.getData();
  expect(result).toBeDefined();
});

// For observables, use firstValueFrom
import { firstValueFrom } from 'rxjs';

it('should emit value', async () => {
  const value = await firstValueFrom(service.getData$());
  expect(value).toBe('expected');
});

// Testing errors
it('should throw on invalid input', async () => {
  await expect(service.process(null)).rejects.toThrow('Invalid input');
});
```

